# Built for Shopify & App Store Review Standards

## 1. Polaris UI & Design Standards
- **Zero Raw HTML**: Never render raw HTML tags (`<div>`, `<p>`, `<span>`, `<h1>`, `<button>`) in the admin interface. Exclusively use `@shopify/polaris` primitives:
  - Page wrapper: `<Page title="..." backAction={...} primaryAction={...}>`
  - Columns: `<Layout><Layout.Section>...</Layout.Section></Layout>`
  - Layout & Stacks: `<BlockStack gap="400">`, `<InlineStack align="space-between">`
  - Content & Actions: `<Card>`, `<Text>`, `<Button>`, `<TextField>`, `<Banner>`, `<Badge>`
- **Loading & Empty States (Required for App Store Review)**:
  - Every table or list MUST implement an `<EmptyState>` when no data exists (e.g., before the merchant receives their first survey response).
  - Every mutation must reflect loading feedback via `<Button loading={...}>` or Polaris `<Spinner>`.
- **Skeleton Page Wrappers**:
  - When loading data asynchronously, wrap loading views in `<SkeletonPage>` and `<SkeletonBodyText>` to prevent layout shift.

## Page shell
Follow the App Home page migration. Put the route title on `s-page` `heading`, the parent link on `slot="breadcrumb-actions"`, and the one page-level action on `slot="primary-action"` with `variant="primary"`. Put the subtitle in the page body as a paragraph. Do not put badges on the page shell; `s-page` has no accessory slot.

## 2. App Bridge v4 Standards
- Top-level merchant alerts and feedback must use `@shopify/app-bridge-react`:
